          {
            "x": 2.23463687150838,
            "y": 13.245033112582782,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Contributions to Pharmacology</strong><br>\nElion's approach to drug development involved understanding the biochemical processes of diseases, which allowed for more targeted and effective pharmaceuticals. Her work helped lay the groundwork for the development of azathioprine, used for organ transplants, and acyclovir, used for viral herpes.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on Human Health</strong><br>\nThe drugs developed by Elion and her colleagues have saved millions of lives worldwide. Her research has had a profound impact on treating various medical conditions, demonstrating the power of scientific inquiry in pharmacology.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Mentoring and Education</strong><br>\nThroughout her career, Elion was dedicated to mentoring young scientists and supporting education in the sciences. She was committed to paving the way for future generations of researchers.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
                "defaultLanguage": "en"
              },
              "subContentId": "3b13867b-feab-4e2e-bfa2-fcc82e4dbff1"
            },
            "alwaysDisplayComments": false,
            "backgroundOpacity": 0,
