            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Recognition and Honorary Degrees</strong><br>\nElion received numerous awards and honors, including 25 honorary degrees from universities around the world. She was also elected to the National Academy of Sciences and the American Academy of Arts and Sciences.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Legacy and Inspirational Role</strong><br>\nElion's work continues to inspire medicinal chemists and biochemists. Her legacy as a pioneer in drug discovery and as a role model for women in science endures beyond her passing on February 21, 1999.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Death and Ongoing Influence</strong><br>\nGertrude B. Elion's passing marked the loss of a groundbreaking scientist whose contributions continue to influence the field of medicine. Her dedication and scientific accomplishments remain a testament to her impact on the world.</p>\n"
              },
              "metadata": {
                "contentType": "Text",
                "license": "U",
                "title": "Unbenannt: Text",
